menu "Sprout feature modules"

# Secure by default: supervising a child's mood is a guardian decision, so the
# device never reports a sample until the feature is compiled in AND the family
# has turned mood sensing on in the parent app. The platform refuses samples
# with 403 while the family switch is off.
config FEATURE_EMOTION_REPORT
    bool "Report emotion observations to the platform"
    default n
    depends on FEATURE_COMPANIONSHIP && FEATURE_DEVICE_BINDING_CLIENT && FEATURE_NETWORK_MANAGER && FEATURE_TIME_SYNC
    help
        Sends one coarse mood sample (label, confidence, observation instant)
        to POST /api/v1/devices/{device_id}/emotion-observations each time the
        companionship module settles on an emotion after a wake or a finished
        turn. No conversation text, audio, or image ever leaves the device.
        Companionship keeps working locally when this is disabled.

config EMOTION_REPORT_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    int "Minimum interval between two reported samples in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_EMOTION_REPORT
    range 30 3600
    default 60
    help
        A child who is awake and chatting produces many turns per minute; a
        sample per turn would turn an aggregate into a minute-by-minute log of
        one child. One sample per minute still gives a weekly distribution.

config EMOTION_REPORT_RETRY_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    int "Retry interval after a transient upload failure in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_EMOTION_REPORT
    range 5 600
    default 30

config EMOTION_REPORT_BACKOFF_MAX_SECONDS
    int "Maximum retry backoff after consecutive failures in seconds"
    depends on FEATURE_EMOTION_REPORT
    range 60 3600
    default 900
    help
        Each consecutive failure doubles the wait between attempts up to this
        ceiling, so a platform outage or an unregistered device stops asking
        instead of retrying on every turn.

config EMOTION_REPORT_QUEUE_CAPACITY
    int "Samples held locally while offline"
    depends on FEATURE_EMOTION_REPORT
    range 0 32
    default 8
    help
        Samples recorded while the device cannot reach the platform wait for
        the next worker cycle. The oldest sample is dropped when the queue is
        full, because a mood distribution is worth more than one old instant
        and every retained sample is retained child data.

endmenu
